From e528e12103efe6304abb53c2ec3a7aca48934a3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alphx61-claude <taranrajput11@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] drm/panel: Add Ilitek ILI9881C SKI550002 panel driver

The Samsung Galaxy On7 (2015) is dual-sourced: next to the Samsung
S6D7AA0X62 BV050HDM it also ships an Ilitek ILI9881C SKI550002 5.5"
720x1280 DSI video mode panel. The init sequence differs enough from
the existing panel-ilitek-ili9881c driver to warrant its own driver.

Generated with linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator from the vendor
device tree.

The vendor device tree claims a 72x129 mm active area, which would make
this a 5.8" panel. The On7 is a 5.5" device sharing the glass with the
S6D7AA0X62 variant, so use the same 68x121 mm instead.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WBT8fxGbtA4EKiL94VBvk2
